+Sign & Verify Server (0021 — 0030)
+=================================
+
+This set provides a minimal remote signing server and client tools. It is intentionally lightweight:
+- FastAPI server in `signing_server/app.py`
+- DB initialization and API key tooling
+- client `graffi/remote_signer_client.py` to publish/query/verify
+- scripts for publishing patches and simple webhook support
+- CI workflow, nginx proxy template, systemd unit and admin key manager
+
+Quick deploy (example, not automated):
+1. Create an install dir (e.g. `/opt/graffi/signing_server`) and copy `signing_server/` and surrounding files there.
+2. Create a Python venv and install runtime deps:
+   python3 -m venv .venv
+   source .venv/bin/activate
+   pip install fastapi uvicorn requests
+3. Initialize DB and create API key:
+   python3 signing_server/init_db.py admin
+   # prints API key; save it
+4. Start server (test):
+   uvicorn signing_server.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
+5. Create nginx config at /etc/nginx/sites-available/signing_server using `deploy/signing_server_nginx.conf` (edit host, certs).
+6. Create systemd unit from `deploy/signing_server.service` (adjust WorkingDirectory), enable & start.
+
+Publishing patches:
+ - Generate patch files as before into `.graffi_helper_model/patches/`.
+ - Ensure `.sig` files exist (use graffi/patch_signer.py sign).
+ - Publish:
+     ./scripts/publish_patch.sh .graffi_helper_model/patches/0001_env_template_secure.patch http://signing.example.com <API_KEY>
+
+Integration with auto-rebuilder:
+ - Set env vars in your environment where ai_rebuilder will run:
+     export GRAFFI_SIGNING_SERVER="https://signing.example.com"
+     export GRAFFI_SIGNING_APIKEY="<not required for read>"
+ - The ai_rebuilder will query the signing server for each patch fingerprint; if the remote fingerprint doesn't match local, it aborts.
+
+Security notes & next steps:
+ - This is a minimal PoC. For production, secure the server with TLS, require stronger auth, rate-limit, add HMAC signing of API responses, and deploy behind a firewall.
+ - Add signed JWT tokens for uploader identity, rotate API keys, and add audit logging.
+ - If you want, I can produce a patch set to add mutual-TLS, signature verification via public-key cryptography (ed25519/PyNaCl), or a verification UI.
+
+Enjoy — save this README next to the server install.

